-**Formulas:**
-
-*   **Volume Rendering Integral (Discrete):**
-    The color $C$ and opacity $A$ are accumulated along the ray. For each sample $i$ with opacity $A_i$ and color $C_i$:
-    $$ C = \sum_{i} C_i A_i \prod_{j < i} (1 - A_j) $$
-    $$ A = 1 - \prod_{i} (1 - A_i) $$
-    [S3, book]
-
-*   **Hardware Blending Equations:**
-    *   **Over Operator (Back-to-Front):**
-        $$ Source = 1 $$
-        $$ Destination = 1 - Source\ Alpha $$
-        [S2, unofficial]
-    *   **Under Operator (Front-to-Back):**
-        $$ Source = 1 - Destination\ Alpha $$
-        $$ Destination = 1 $$
-        [S2, unofficial]
-
-*   **Normal Estimation (for Illumination):**
-    Using central differences with step $\delta$ (e.g., $1/256.0$):
-    $$ N_x = \text{tex3D}(P + (\delta, 0, 0)) - \text{tex3D}(P - (\delta, 0, 0)) $$
-    $$ N_y = \text{tex3D}(P + (0, \delta, 0)) - \text{tex3D}(P - (0, \delta, 0)) $$
-    $$ N_z = \text{tex3D}(P + (0, 0, \delta)) - \text{tex3D}(P - (0, 0, \delta)) $$
-    $$ N = \text{normalize}(N_x, N_y, N_z) $$
-    [S5, unofficial]
-
-*   **Blinn-Phong Shading:**
-    $$ H = \text{normalize}(L + V) $$
-    $$ Ambient = K_a \cdot L_{ambient} $$
-    $$ Diffuse = K_d \cdot L_{color} \cdot \max(0, L \cdot N) $$
-    $$ Specular = K_s \cdot L_{color} \cdot \max(0, H \cdot N)^{shininess} $$
-    $$ Result = Ambient + Diffuse + Specular $$
-    [S2, S5, unofficial]
-
-**Parameters:**
-*   **Slice Increment (PLANE_INC):** Controls the distance between proxy planes. Initialized to 1.0 in some implementations [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Threshold (u_thresh):** Scalar value below which fragments are discarded [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Alpha Scale (u_alphaScale):** Multiplier for fragment alpha in transparent mode [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Shading Constants:** $K_a=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, $K_d=(0.6,0.6,0.6)$, $K_s=(0.2,0.2,0.2)$, shininess=100.0 [S5, unofficial].
-
-**Pseudocode:**
+    *   Specify shader input parameters (matrices, uniforms) [S9].
+    *   Draw slice polygons in sorted order (back-to-front for Over operator) [S2, unofficial][S3, book].
+    *   Restore rendering state [S3, book].
+
+### Fragment Shader Execution
+For each fragment of a proxy polygon:
+1.  **Interpolate Texture Coordinates:** Receive interpolated 3D texture coordinates from vertex attributes [S3, book].
+2.  **Data Lookup:** Sample the volume texture at the interpolated coordinates to retrieve the scalar value $v$ [S3, book].
+    *   *Note:* If using 2D textures, bilinear interpolation is used within slices, causing artifacts at slice boundaries [S8, unofficial]. 3D textures use trilinear interpolation [S1, unofficial].
+3.  **Transfer Function Lookup:** Use the scalar value $v$ as a texture coordinate for a dependent lookup into the 1D transfer function texture to retrieve color $C$ and opacity $\alpha$ [S3, book].
+4.  **Illumination (Optional):**
+    *   Compute surface normal using central differences (finite differences) between neighboring voxels [S2, S6, unofficial].
+    *   Apply lighting model (e.g., Blinn-Phong) to modify color [S2, S5, unofficial].
+5.  **Compositing:** The resulting color and alpha are sent to the hardware compositing stage (alpha blending) [S2, unofficial][S3, book].
